<title>USA: U.S. car and truck sales for month of October.</title>
<headline>U.S. car and truck sales for month of October.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following chart represents U.S. sales of cars and trucks for October, as reported by individual automakers.</p>
<p>Percentage changes are based on daily selling rates. Market shares also are expressed as a percentage of the total market. The sales figures include imported cars and trucks sold in the United States.</p>
<p> Maker		Cars    Pct   Share  Trucks     Pct   Share</p>
<p> GM		213,798  -23.9    31.5 185,584   +22.2    31.4</p>
<p> Ford	    143,191   -3.9    21.1 191,399    +8.3    32.4</p>
<p> Chrysler	 61,213  +12.9     9.0 144,180   +22.3    24.4</p>
<p> Toyota	   62,276   +7.2     9.2  30,642   +38.0     5.2</p>
<p> Honda	    71,310  +11.0    10.5   3,604   -22.0     0.6</p>
<p> Nissan	   31,597  -10.6     4.7  17,524   -13.9     3.0</p>
<p> Mazda	    11,266  -26.3     1.7   3,706   -14.7     0.6</p>
<p> Mitsubishi     17,497  +12.3     2.6   1,691    -9.0     0.3</p>
<p> Isuzu		   0   N.A.    N.A.   7,722   -13.7     1.3</p>
<p> Subaru	   11,966  +19.3     1.8	 0    N.A.     N.A.</p>
<p> Hyundai	   9,075  +11.8     1.3	 0    N.A.     N.A.</p>
<p> Volkswagen	9,959  +36.0     1.5	71    -29.5    0.0</p>
<p> Volvo	     7,067   +2.5     1.0	 0    N.A.     N.A.</p>
<p> Mercedes	  8,259  +68.4     1.2	 0    N.A.     N.A.</p>
<p> BMW		10,076  +25.5     1.5	 0    N.A.     N.A.</p>
<p> Saab		1,478  -39.7     0.2	 0    N.A.     N.A.</p>
<p> Suzuki		600  -61.4     0.1   2,748    +25.2    0.5</p>
<p> Audi		2,170  +11.5     0.3	 0    N.A.     N.A.</p>
<p> Jaguar	    2,254  +63.2     0.3	 0    N.A.     N.A.</p>
<p> Porsche	     619  +33.6     0.1	 0    N.A.     N.A.</p>
